# Tested-version lock for the LLM-engine CLIs ctxloom's importers
# (internal/transcript/importer/{codex,claude,kiro}) are known to
# parse correctly. This is a SIBLING of .devcontainer/tool-versions.env, not
# an addition to it: that file pins build/codegen tooling into the devcontainer
# image build (Go, buf, versionator, …) and is drift-gated 1:1 against the
# Dockerfile/justfile/CI by internal/buildpins. Engine CLIs are not installed
# in that image and don't belong in its build-arg contract — see the plan's
# Decision A. This file's own drift gate is internal/enginepins.
#
# Consumer: .github/workflows/engine-drift-detect.yml (scheduled) resolves
# each engine's latest published CLI version from its release feed and
# compares it against the value pinned here. A mismatch means a version
# ctxloom's parser has never seen has shipped — the workflow opens/labels a
# tracking issue (alert-only; P0 of the self-healing pipeline). Later phases
# (P1+) will have the pipeline bump these values itself after a successful
# capture + drift-oracle run; for now they are bumped by hand when a human
# confirms the importer still parses the new version's transcripts.
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, one per line, `#` comment/blank lines allowed —
# same convention as tool-versions.env. No quoting, no export statements.
#
# Seed values below are the latest published version of each engine CLI as of
# 2026-07-18 (npm `@anthropic-ai/claude-code`/`@openai/codex`;
# kiro.dev/changelog/cli/ for kiro-cli, pinned to its 2.x stable track, not
# the 3.x `--v3` early-access track) — they are a starting placeholder, not a
# guarantee the importer has been re-validated against them; treat the first
# drift-detect run as the thing that proves (or disproves) each one.
CODEX_CLI_VERSION=0.144.6
CLAUDE_CODE_CLI_VERSION=2.1.214
KIRO_CLI_VERSION=2.13.0
